WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.450
Hands up if you’ve used AI today.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.130
Only three of you?

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.060
I’d say every one of you has, and

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.220
before you even got to school!

5
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.620
Today: what AI is, where you

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.580
meet it, and what it isn’t.

7
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.580
Some machines only follow

8
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.300
rules that a person wrote.

9
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.560
Your alarm rings at six

10
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.380
because you set it for six.

11
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.230
A calculator gives the same answer

12
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.610
to the same sum, every time.

13
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.010
Useful, but they never learn anything new.

14
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.280
Other machines learn from examples.

15
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.310
Watch two football clips, and your

16
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.910
video app lines up a third.

17
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.950
Nobody wrote that rule just for you.

18
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.130
The app learned from what

19
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.910
millions of people watched next,

20
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.070
and it made a guess about you.

21
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.840
So here’s what most people

22
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.320
mean by AI today.

23
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.860
It’s a computer system that learns

24
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.900
patterns from lots of examples.

25
00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.810
Then it uses those patterns to make

26
00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.050
predictions: best guesses about

27
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.350
things it doesn’t know yet.

28
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.830
Think of a goalkeeper facing a penalty.

29
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.320
She’s watched this striker take twenty

30
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.780
penalties, and most went to the left.

31
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.860
So she dives left.

32
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.130
That’s a prediction from patterns.

33
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.980
It isn’t mind reading, and

34
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.120
sometimes she’s wrong.

35
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:23.850
Quick check!

36
00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.130
A street light switches on

37
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.810
at six every evening.

38
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.500
A map app warns that your bus

39
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.820
route is slow today.

40
00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.370
Which one is AI?

41
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.780
The map app.

42
00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.250
It learned from the trips of millions

43
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.110
of phones how traffic usually moves,

44
00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.110
and it predicts today’s delays.

45
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.560
The street light just follows a

46
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.800
timer that someone set.

47
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.450
Now think about your morning again.

48
00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.990
Face unlock learned from many

49
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:54.910
faces how to tell yours apart.

50
00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.000
Your keyboard guesses your next word.

51
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.620
Voice notes can be turned into text.

52
00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.590
And a spam filter hides scam

53
00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.490
messages before you see them.

54
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.720
But AI doesn’t think or

55
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.820
feel the way you do.

56
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:13.770
When a chatbot writes “I understand”, it’s

57
00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.850
predicting words that usually fit.

58
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.070
It has no feelings, and it doesn’t

59
00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.510
know what’s true in your life.

60
00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.660
After this video, open the lab.

61
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.480
You’ll see the start of a sentence: “In

62
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.880
the morning the pupils open their”.

63
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.410
Bars show how likely each next word is:

64
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.550
books, notebooks, windows or phones.

65
00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.060
Move the temperature slider, and watch the

66
00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.360
choices get safer or more surprising.

67
00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.410
Your turn.

68
00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.580
A chatbot writes, “I’m so

69
00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.740
happy to help you!”

70
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.980
Does it really feel happy?

71
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.430
No: it predicts words that

72
00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.650
fit, but it feels nothing.

73
00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.900
Remember: some machines only follow rules,

74
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.180
while AI learns patterns from examples.

75
00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.870
What AI gives you is a

76
00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.730
prediction, a best guess.

77
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.240
And best guesses can be wrong.

78
00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.520
Try it yourself: keep an AI

79
00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.060
diary for one day.

80
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.010
Every time you meet AI, on your

81
00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.990
keyboard, a map or a video app,

82
00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:22.550
write down what it predicted.

83
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.590
Then ask yourself: was it right?
